The earlier opening was aboard ship, but the last session stopped on the docks with Tamsin writing and the slate man waiting, so this one stays there. Result 1: "Follow Balance" can be read as Mira trying to keep things even, tallying what she owes against what she's holding, matching up her ledger-minded surroundings. Result 2: "Unnatural Facility" is the relay console, a facility that works with eerie smoothness.

Tamsin's pen keeps writing, and you stand there trying to keep things even: what you owe against what you've left, the slip, the manifest, the promise. The sums do not come out, and you check them twice anyway. Past her shoulder the relay console glows with a steady, unhurried efficiency that nothing else on the docks can claim. The man with the slate is still waiting, and he is starting to look like furniture that has learned to sigh. "Take your time," Tamsin says, not looking up, in the voice of someone who is counting yours. You keep adding, and the docks keep their own books.

